      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_DETAIL\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- average number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- standard deviation of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- courses with at least one associated course material: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- subject ID: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\n- subject title: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- subjects in the 'Engineering' school: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SCHOOL_NAME\n- total units equal to 1: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- term description: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION\n- subject rank within academic year: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n\n## Join Keys\n- TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, give the department name and find the average and standard deviation of the number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated course material.\n```sql\nSELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment, STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrollment_stddev FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID WHERE td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY <> 'NM' GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME ORDER BY enrollment_stddev DESC;\n```\n2. For subjects in the \"Engineering\" school with total units equal to 1, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, academic year, and the rank of each subject within its academic year group ordered by subject ID.\n```sql\nSELECT t1.SUBJECT_ID, t1.SUBJECT_TITLE, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t2.ACADEMIC_YEAR, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t2.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY t1.SUBJECT_ID) AS window_column FROM SUBJECT_SUMMARY t1 INNER JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL t0 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE INNER JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t2 ON t1.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE WHERE t1.SCHOOL_NAME = 'Engineering' AND t1.TOTAL_UNITS = 1\n```\n3. For each department, give the department name, the average and standard deviation of the number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated course material, and for subjects in the \"Engineering\" school with total units equal to 1 in that department, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, academic year, and the rank of each subject within its academic year group ordered by subject ID. Present the results ordered by the enrollment standard deviation in descending order, then by academic year and subject rank.\n```sql\nWITH DeptEnrollmentStats AS ( SELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment, STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrollment_stddev FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID WHERE td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY <> 'NM' GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME ORDER BY enrollment_stddev DESC ), EngineeringSubjects AS ( SELECT t1.SUBJECT_ID, t1.SUBJECT_TITLE, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t2.ACADEMIC_YEAR, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t2.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY t1.SUBJECT_ID) AS window_column FROM SUBJECT_SUMMARY t1 INNER JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL t0 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE INNER JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t2 ON t1.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE WHERE t1.SCHOOL_NAME = 'Engineering' AND t1.TOTAL_UNITS = 1 ) SELECT des.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, des.avg_enrollment, des.enrollment_stddev, es.SUBJECT_ID, es.SUBJECT_TITLE, es.DEPARTMENT_NAME, es.ACADEMIC_YEAR, es.window_column FROM DeptEnrollmentStats des JOIN EngineeringSubjects es ON des.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = es.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY des.enrollment_stddev DESC, es.ACADEMIC_YEAR, es.window_column;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department, provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated course material. Additionally, for subjects in the \"Engineering\" school with total units equal to 1 in that department, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, academic year, the rank of each subject within its academic year group ordered by subject ID, and the term description for each subject. Present the results ordered by the enrollment standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) in descending order, then by academic year and subject rank. Do not return any rounded answers."
